  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 235 PM EDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nThe extended period begins Wed with an upper ridge centered over the \nTN/North GA/Western NC, along with a surface ridge/wedge nosing down \nthe eastern seaboard from the New England states. By Wed morning the \nwedge will be firmly entrenched into North and Central GA with East \nto SE winds in the 8-12mph range. By Wed the drier airmass will be \nfiltering into east central GA with dewpoints expected in the upper \n50s and lower 60s. This drier airmass continues into Thu and moves \nnorthward bringing those lower 60s dewpoints in across all of north \nand central GA. High temps stay in the upper 80s to lower 90s \nthrough the end of the week but with the drier air moving in Heat \nIndex values will drop from the upper 90s to lower 100s Tue to the \nlower 90s Wed to Fri. \n\nModels show moisture beginning to return Fri evening into Sat as the \nridge finally begins to break down. The continued east to \nsoutheasterly flow brings atlantic moisture in across the state as \nwe get into the weekend. Right now just going with a 20% to 30% \nchance of showers and thunderstorms Sat and Sun.",
